t as 2 requests? The \"requests_left\" refers model API calls, and tool calls inside one action are not model requests. But each tool result returns to model as feedback, potentially one executor output. The contract says \"Briefly describe next action, then output ONE fenced Python block\". We can make multiple independent tool calls in one block. Group independent operations. Great: call run_command for page 9-10 and page 50-52 in one block, print filtered text around keywords. That's one action.\n\nBut careful: run_command cwd '.' argv list. Let's do:\n\nimport json\nr1=run_command([\"python\",\"read_pdf.py\",\"--start-page\",\"9\",\"--end-page\",\"10\"],\".\")\nprint(r1['rc'], len(r1['stdout']))\nd=json.loads(r1['stdout']); for p in d['pages']: print(page, text[:...]) — we need self-consistency passage; print text around \"Self-consistency\" or \"majority\".\nr2 page 50-52; print around \"Table 4\" and \"Conclusion\" / \"benefit\".\n\nNeed not print all. We can search keywords. Let's do that.\n\nAlso maybe Table 4 on page 50? Let's fetch 50-52.\n\nLet's build the code with keyword windows. Ensure output bounded. We'll print maybe 2500 chars each.\n\nAlso perhaps need page 12/13 for ToT already have. Good.\n\nLet's run."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":8142,"completion_tokens":2618,"total_tokens":10760,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":4224},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":2308},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":4224,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":3918},"system_fingerprint":"bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6"}